#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""agent-brief — the estate briefing engine.

The panel's brain: joins GitHub PR attention, the manna board, live coord
presence, session history, and git into ranked threads, a delta since the
caller's last look, one-tap suggestions carried as data (never executed),
and a paragraph whose every sentence cites a receipt.

Design source of truth (read it before changing shapes):
  holy-ghostty repo, .dev/session-prompts/10-INTELLIGENT-INBOX.md (sibling checkout)

The honesty covenant, non-negotiable:
  - every assertion carries a receipt id (commit hash, mn-id, PR ref, event id)
  - unknown stays unknown; a degraded source is an annotation, never a guess
    and never silence
  - no model output enters the contract unless grounded in the structured
    inputs; a paragraph citing a receipt the engine never issued is rejected
  - numbers come from the joined data, never the model

The contract is versioned and FULL SHAPE from day one: a capability that is
not yet live ships as an honest degradation in the payload (for example
ranking.mode = "heuristic"), never as an absent field, so consumers render
one contract forever.
"""

